<Project>
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <TreatWarningsAsErrors>true</TreatWarningsAsErrors>
    <Deterministic>true</Deterministic>
    <ManagePackageVersionsCentrally>true</ManagePackageVersionsCentrally>
    <RootNamespace>$(MSBuildProjectName)</RootNamespace>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
    <!-- the packages carry XML documentation. The missing-comment warning is off here, and back on
         for Maniacal.Scumm, whose public API is documented in full. (The SDK derives the
         documentation file name before Directory.Build.targets is read, so this lives here.) -->
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);CS1591</NoWarn>
    <ContinuousIntegrationBuild Condition="'$(CI)' == 'true'">true</ContinuousIntegrationBuild>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <PropertyGroup>
    <Product>Maniacal</Product>
    <Authors>Maniacal contributors</Authors>
    <Copyright>Copyright (c) Maniacal contributors. Portions derived from ScummVM, copyright the ScummVM Team, and from Daventry, copyright the Daventry contributors.</Copyright>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>GPL-3.0-or-later</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/jeffnyman/maniacal</RepositoryUrl>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/jeffnyman/maniacal</PackageProjectUrl>
    <!-- dotnet pack -p:VersionSuffix=alpha.2 for the next prerelease; an empty suffix is a release -->
    <VersionPrefix>0.2.0</VersionPrefix>
    <VersionSuffix>alpha</VersionSuffix>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <PackageTags>scumm;maniac-mansion;lucasfilm;c64;adventure;interpreter;scummvm;retro;games</PackageTags>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>Second prerelease: the library's public API, settled for a 1.0. It breaks code written against 0.1.0-alpha. The engine's internals (the script engine, actors, sound players, decoders, renderers, resource index, save serializer) are no longer public. GameWorld is the way to play headless: boot, step, screen, input, saves and loads, and new CopyProtection, Audio, SkipCutscene, Variables and SetVariable, CurrentScript, RunningScripts and ActorsHere. GameInspector (Maniacal.Scumm.Inspection) is new: room pictures with their objects, costumes' figures, scripts decoded, and a room's screen with figures standing in it. Every public member is documented. The maniacal tool plays as before; its --room, --costume, --script and --view are built on the inspection API. Built and tested on Windows, Linux and macOS.</PackageReleaseNotes>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(IsPackable)' == 'true'">
    <None Include="$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="/" Visible="false" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
